+# Isolated initial-pressure experiment
+
+Author: Puma. Status: local experimental patch, not an upstream release.
+Base: 34235d33c886aa05b5bdf95d920b863d1fb2ad6f.
+
+Admission: the separate Rheon Surrogate Lab's preregistered 500-step global
+candidate passed its development-only initial-guess signal. Add one explicit
+sealed-domain initial-pressure RHS entry point. Preserve both existing zero-start
+entry points and preconditioners. No changes to simulation acceptance, operator,
+solver math, dependencies, main branch, or free-surface behavior.
+
+Acceptance: initial pressure is finite, shape-exact and cell-zero gauge-valid;
+full initial r=b-Ap participates in stopping; original b determines relative
+tolerance; Krylov scratch resets. Both preconditioners must pass zero-equivalence,
+exact/poor/invalid guesses, original-b tolerance, full gauge-row gate, repeated
+reuse after cancellation/failure and actual f32 divergence tests. Free-surface
+initial guesses return an explicit unsupported-domain error. Existing numerical
+contracts must continue passing. No heap arrays are added to the workspace.
+
+Allowed write set: src/pressure.rs, tests/initial_pressure_contract.rs and this
+plan. Evidence: cargo fmt --check, cargo test --no-default-features --locked and
+cargo clippy --no-default-features --all-targets --locked -- -D warnings. The lab
+owns the independent review and corrected-solve probe report. This patch is held
+locally and exported as a reviewable diff; the lab's upstream git pin is unchanged.
